{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388575-mage-and-typemoon","id":1388575,"title":"Mage and Typemoon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-14T22:54:07-07:00","id":1388575,"title":"Mage and Typemoon?","content":"Sorry I don't know how many of you know both of them, but at least there is a consensus in Chinese fans: Typemoon, especially early stuff, is greatly influenced by CWoD, especially MtA. And both of them have many similiarities, although Typemoon has developed its own fashion now, but that is true during early time<br /> <br /> But AFAIK there is no discussion or article which is very specific about <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">comparing both of them</span></span></span></div>. So do you know any stuff like this? I want to see it. All languages are welcomed<br /> <br /> Thanks very much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T23:03:08-07:00","id":1388577,"title":"","content":"So far as I know, Nasu has never stated that he was influenced specifically by Mage or the World of Darkness, but there are certainly a lot of parallels between the two and it's not too hard to take material from Type-Moon and slot it into the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T23:28:42-07:00","id":1388584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388575-mage-and-typemoon?p=1388577#post1388577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far as I know, Nasu has never stated that he was influenced specifically by Mage or the World of Darkness, but there are certainly a lot of parallels between the two and it's not too hard to take material from Type-Moon and slot it into the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>A very strange thing, all guys who I meet and know Typemoon, Mage and WoD a bit agree he is greatly influenced by WoD especially Mage. But Nasu himself never stated this in public, well<br /> <br /> I want to see stuff dicussing both of them, their similarities, differences and so on.. it is pity materials about this are few","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T23:30:14-07:00","id":1388585,"title":"","content":"Many TP settings also resemble WoD a lot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T19:53:31-07:00","id":1388826,"title":"","content":"Mind you the WOD didn't come fully formed into existance but like many things was based on previous ideas it wouldn't be hard to believe that similar ideas lead to similar growths though for example magic and science aren't two parts of the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T23:04:37-07:00","id":1388851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388575-mage-and-typemoon?p=1388826#post1388826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you the WOD didn't come fully formed into existance but like many things was based on previous ideas it wouldn't be hard to believe that similar ideas lead to similar growths though for example magic and science aren't two parts of the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is necessary to find out how many similarities of both are pioneered by WoD particularly <br /> <br /> For example, Typemoon has a concept which is very similar to Paradox: Mystery will be weakened if it is exposed to Consensus<br /> <br /> To be honest I haven\u2019t seen any setting before WoD which is very close to Paradox of MtA. No one has a concept which is so specific. This makes us think Nasu refers to MtA<br /> <br /> But others, like the concept of Realms, Umbra or all Otherworlds, may not come from WoD solely, most fantasies like DnD also have this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T23:18:17-07:00","id":1388853,"title":"","content":"Nasu is used to be a TRPG gamer, it is unbelievable he didn\u2019t be exposed to WoD, which was much more popular in 90s. But his interview didn\u2019t mention a word about WoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T08:03:18-07:00","id":1388944,"title":"","content":"Interesting I didn't know Tabletop gaming influenced Typemoon, I mean it makes sense but its always hard to tell. Like Miyazaki from Fromsoft was a fan of Fighting Fantasy Novels and they inspired a lot of his games, but in interviews it is found he is also a fan of Magic the Gathering, DnD, and Call of Chthulhu boardgames. And Fighting Fantasy was before my time so I didn't realize it greatly influenced the Japanese RPG scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T08:16:48-07:00","id":1388947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1388575-mage-and-typemoon?p=1388944#post1388944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting I didn't know Tabletop gaming influenced Typemoon, I mean it makes sense but its always hard to tell. Like Miyazaki from Fromsoft was a fan of Fighting Fantasy Novels and they inspired a lot of his games, but in interviews it is found he is also a fan of Magic the Gathering, DnD, and Call of Chthulhu boardgames. And Fighting Fantasy was before my time so I didn't realize it greatly influenced the Japanese RPG scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>TRPGs Nasu himself mentioned were DnD, Tunnels &amp; Trolls and the one I forget the name now, but in general he played american ones most. He also played janpanese TRPGs, maybe some of them refer to WoD...<br /> <br /> But again, it is hard to believe he didn\u2019t know or have a scratch or play the WoD, which is very popular at that time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T08:27:52-07:00","id":1388949,"title":"","content":"No definitely. Like I could see the influence in the first Hellsing OVA when they made that Setite Incognito.<br /> <br /> And Witch Hunter Robin and the use of the term Methuselahs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}